Nesting and branches
A nesting block (If, for example) has a vertical bar on its left; drag a block to the right of that bar and it becomes its child;
children can nest further, with no depth limit.

[b]Note[/b]: If is a pure container — it does not take up a line of its own on export, and the blocks in its nest are laid out flat in order.
Use [b]Jump[/b] when you need a real conditional branch.